<title>USA: TABLE-Corrections Q2 net income up 66 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Corrections Q2 net income up 66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corrections Corporation Of America</p>
<p>				Three Months ended  Six months ended</p>
<p>				     June 30		June 30</p>
<p>				1997	1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p> Revenues		$107,024   $67,453   $198,862   $130,730</p>
<p> Operating income	19,971    12,495     40,372     23,386</p>
<p> Net income		11,612     7,007     23,607     12,713</p>
<p>Net income per share:</p>
<p>  Primary		    0.14	0.09	 0.28	 0.16</p>
<p>  Fully diluted	    0.13	0.08	 0.27	 0.15</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding</p>
<p>  Primary		  84,411    82,001     84,197     81,065</p>
<p>  Fully diluted	  90,318    86,361     90,199     85,671</p>
<p>Beds in operation (end of quarter)</p>
<p>			     32,441    20,994     32,441     20,994</p>
<p> Average occupancy	93.1%     93.8%	93.8%	91.6%</p>
<p>			  (000s except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Company says Q2 1997 results include $1.4 million after-tax loss because of CAA's departure from two management contracts on June 30.</p>
<p>Co says Q2 net income wouldhave been approcimately $13.0 million, or $0.15 per fully diluted share without the losses from contracts in Sante Fe, N.M. and Columbia, S.C.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
